1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,240
Episode 2

2
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:14,700
Where'd a Jaggy go?

3
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:16,744
Don't tell me he's sleeping in.

4
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:19,140
We have an escaped inmate!

5
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,140
Hunt out, use this kid and capture him!

6
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:24,110
Wado?!

7
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:33,517
One dream, one wish.

8
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,160
If you want it, gotta go over the top.

9
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:57,680
Setting sail and heading for the unknown.

10
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:02,300
Cutting through the
winds and waves as I go.

11
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:05,357
Gotta keep it up, never stopping, no.

12
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,777
Cause I'm aiming to get there first, yeah.

13
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:10,337
It's all or nothing, no time to worry.

14
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:13,160
Do it later, right now I'm living free.

15
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:20,357
When your foes look like
they will overwhelm you.

16
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:25,120
It means your heart's saying
this is what you can't do.

17
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:28,497
Despite all that to run is not an option.

18
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:30,597
Once they're close to
feel the satisfaction.

19
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:32,857
You think I'm rude,
here's my appreciation.

20
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:35,860
When things are getting
tough, just gotta smile.

21
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:41,237
If you are going on your way.

22
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:43,497
And you're looking for
a fresh, brand new day.

23
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:46,637
Then make sure your only
thought you have is.

24
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:48,077
Yes, I can.

25
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:53,237
As you're on your way,
marks maps will be made.

26
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:56,220
Yes, with every step that you will take.

27
00:01:56,940 --> 00:01:59,317
Just look at all you've been through.

28
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,577
Look ahead at new horizons in view.

29
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:05,840
Shining brightly, oh, who
knows what's waiting for you.

30
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:09,057
Dream living, that's the way.

31
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:11,097
Make like a hurricane.

32
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:14,140
Now, got to make your mark today.

33
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:20,097
One dream, one wish.

34
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:21,917
Your dreams don't run away.

35
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,857
Go for the knockout.

36
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:27,040
Over the top.

37
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:32,640
Reliquity lost that round, huh?

38
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,357
And Mama as well.

39
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:36,837
She could be anywhere
after falling like that.

40
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,997
If we try climbing the waterfall.

41
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,797
He will just kick us down again.

42
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:43,200
That was one hell of a tumble!

43
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:45,917
I can't believe we
survived without a scratch.

44
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,882
It's a miracle that Chanta
landed right side off.

45
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,060
So, we're just supposed to wait?

46
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:52,300
I'm afraid so.

47
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:56,457
If any of us power users fall off
the ship, we'll be as good as dead.

48
00:02:56,540 --> 00:02:57,370
Hold on!

49
00:02:57,453 --> 00:02:59,654
You think that's what happened to Mama?

50
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,680
I wouldn't worry.

51
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:04,360
I checked Mama's Vivre card.

52
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:08,097
Unfortunately, it says she's
still among the Lickety Living.

53
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:09,237
So she didn't drown?

54
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:10,150
That's awesome!

55
00:03:10,233 --> 00:03:11,877
But there's just water down there.

56
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:12,790
Where'd she go?

57
00:03:12,873 --> 00:03:13,703
Good point.

58
00:03:13,786 --> 00:03:15,957
That probably means the
Beast Pirates hauled her

59
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:18,217
up from the sea and
locked her away somewhere.

60
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:19,712
That complicates things.

61
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,606
What do you think they'll do?

62
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:24,580
Mom and Kaido were
crewmates many years ago.

63
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:29,257
But since they're both emperors now, they're
only interested in coming out on top.

64
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:32,480
In other words, they'll kill her for sure.

65
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:35,680
Then what's gonna happen to us?

66
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:42,440
The era of the big mom pirates will end.

67
00:03:42,740 --> 00:03:46,387
Because they'll become the Pharaoh
Sparrow Pirates, of course.

68
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:47,780
Hold on.

69
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,317
Is that some kind of joke?

70
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:52,297
Because the next captain
should obviously be Katakuri.

71
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:54,420
But our crew values seniority.

72
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:56,460
Quality is what we need.

73
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:59,577
The eldest son should be the
Lickety Leader, you fool.

74
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:00,542
You are a fool.

75
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:03,540
I'll do it. Don't cut it out.

76
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:06,180
Mama won't die so easily.

77
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:08,406
She's not some mere commoner.

78
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:09,995
She'll keep fighting.

79
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:14,120
Who is Big Mom? A friend.

80
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:16,500
She's a strong lady from overseas.

81
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:18,800
Mom, ma-ma-ma-ma.

82
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:23,415
This shark-a-dile is so tame and
sweet, it even lets us run on its back.

83
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:28,420
Yeah, after you pounded
it on the head twice.

84
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:31,757
Wait, but why are you going
into Udon with this woman?

85
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:34,457
Nothing you're saying
makes a bit of sense to me.

86
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:38,220
I told you she's real strong,
so she'll help us save Big Bro.

87
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:40,600
This is making my head spin.

88
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:42,557
Just come back for now, please.

89
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:44,517
Then we can work all of this out.

90
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:46,557
Sir Kin'emon has left me with a mission.

91
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:50,937
I was to guard Lord Momonosuke in his
absence, as if my life depended on it.

92
00:04:51,020 --> 00:04:52,060
Don't you worry.

93
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,440
I got this.

94
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:58,200
On my honor as a kunoichi, I vow that
no harm will come to the young lord.

95
00:04:58,580 --> 00:04:59,560
What honor?

96
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:02,177
You've barely even started your training.

97
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,917
You can't even protect yourself.

98
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:08,941
Stop being ridiculous and return home before
something bad happens to you yet again.

99
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:12,700
Sir Hitetsu, I'm afraid
we're already on our way.

100
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:15,420
Well, turn back. I beg of you.

101
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:18,140
Be reasonable, Lady Okiku. Take care.

102
00:05:18,260 --> 00:05:19,137
Come and see you for me.

103
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:20,240
Bye. Da-lick.

104
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:25,242
There's something you just said.

105
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:28,037
The name Big Mom sounds
awfully familiar to me.

106
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,640
Who could that be?

107
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,460
Never mind, Olene.

108
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,149
Your friends were so nice.

109
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:35,020
I had fun in Okobore town.

110
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:36,672
They're all so generous.

111
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:38,600
They don't know who I am.

112
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,540
I don't know who I am.

113
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:45,460
But they welcomed me like a guest and
even gave me a sweet treat to eat.

114
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:48,271
Her talking hat hasn't said a single word.

115
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:50,717
Does that mean it's lost its memory, too?

116
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:53,480
It's all coming back to me now.

117
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:56,897
The flavor of that sweet
soup melting in my mouth.

118
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:58,200
Don't look at me!

119
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:00,620
I can't help it, Topper-Abon.

120
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:03,377
You're so cute and sweet,
I could just eat you up.

121
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:05,200
How dare you! I'm not food!

122
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,680
You're working hard, Momo. I'm impressed.

123
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:10,260
I must stay sharp.

124
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:13,305
I am at the center of
this conflict, after all.

125
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:15,230
Tsunachi!

126
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:17,250
I'm sorry.

127
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:18,891
Most inconsiderate of me.

128
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:23,377
By the way, what's that thing you
say when you swing your sword?

129
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:25,397
Tsunachi or something, it sounds like?

130
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:26,310
That's correct.

131
00:06:26,393 --> 00:06:28,917
It is a word that fills you with energy,

132
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:36,000
that's

133
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:44,690
quite enough,

134
00:06:44,773 --> 00:06:45,603
both of you.

135
00:06:45,686 --> 00:06:46,777
What's the matter?

136
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:48,957
Where did you learn such a word?

137
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:50,737
It's what they yell in sword fights.

138
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:54,317
Overseas, Zoro Giri taught it to me.

139
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:56,177
He says it's a good luck word to.

140
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:58,837
uplift your spirit when
your courage falters.

141
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:02,760
Then I forbid you to
say it. What? But why?

142
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:04,997
Perhaps it's merely a coincidence,

143
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:08,315
but the same word was once
used in an old Kuri dialect.

144
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:12,440
It's not appropriate for a person
of your standing to say. Why?

145
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:13,617
What harm does it do?

146
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:14,530
No.

147
00:07:14,613 --> 00:07:16,817
But it gives you energy
and I think it's me.

148
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:18,640
I'm afraid no means no.

149
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:23,040
I'm positively famished.

150
00:07:23,260 --> 00:07:25,737
Tell me we've made it
to Udon and I can eat.

151
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:28,620
I could really use a snack, you know.

152
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:32,157
Don't drool and talk about
snacks when you look at me!

153
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:36,358
I'm sorry, Oline, but I'm afraid we
still have quite a long way to go.

154
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:37,680
Oh, surely not!

155
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:42,037
I'll show you a rough
map of the land of Wano.

156
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:46,257
As you can see, we have six regions, each
with a different climate than the next.

157
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:50,281
They're divided by a river that
stretches across the entire island.

158
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:09,780
colored rice a secret message from
shinobu no doubt wait at the dried up well

159
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:16,277
that seems convenient
enough i am relieved to find

160
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:19,597
you in good health though
your pursuers must have been

161
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:22,537
persistent indeed if you fled
all the way here to ringo

162
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:26,340
but rest assured Orochi's
men will not follow this far.

163
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:30,057
I'm still shocked that
they would kill Komurasaki.

164
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:32,060
She was quite beloved. Yes.

165
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:35,577
The incident has thrown the
flower capital into an uproar.

166
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:36,490
It's sick.

167
00:08:36,573 --> 00:08:38,305
She wasn't a threat to anyone.

168
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:42,226
But the second she stood up to
Orochi, they cut her right down.

169
00:08:43,740 --> 00:08:45,034
Samurai, you're scary.

170
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:49,302
The man who killed her is a Yakuza
boss known as Napping Kyoshiro.

171
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:50,610
Kyoshiro?

172
00:08:50,693 --> 00:08:52,857
The name is not familiar to me.

173
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:57,920
Though I am quite familiar with the most
famous Yakuza boss from 20 years ago.

174
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:01,780
He was called Hiogoro the Flower.

175
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:06,497
A rather extravagant name, but I like it.

176
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:07,617
Times have changed.

177
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:10,237
Hiogoro was a man of
honor who helped the weak.

178
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:12,857
He would never have
done such a cruel thing.

179
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:14,440
A shame he wasn't there.

180
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:21,060
It sounds like this Kyoshiro fellow
is quite the loathsome beast!

181
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:26,037
In that case, perhaps we shouldn't have
taken Otoko back to his pleasure hall.

182
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:28,826
Surely what he did was
just a show of loyalty.

183
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,577
You'd think he would go out of his way to

184
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:33,425
kill a child over a minor
infraction like that?

185
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:38,140
Well, he killed the Oiron who worked
for him, and she was a superstar.

186
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,560
It worries me.

187
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:42,420
We should check on her. Let's go back.

188
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:45,420
Don't catch a cold.

189
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,877
That's so much better.

190
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:48,078
Thank you, Shinobu.

191
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:50,350
Here's a thought.

192
00:09:50,433 --> 00:09:52,377
If we're headed back to the capital,

193
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:56,517
let's have a nice warm soak in one of
their bathhouses to rest our weary bones.

194
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:57,430
I'm sold.

195
00:09:57,513 --> 00:09:59,240
I can't wait. I agree.

196
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:01,277
It'll be a nice change of pace.

197
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:02,660
We'll need disguises.

198
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:05,717
Orochi controls every
aspect of the capital.

199
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:09,357
In other words, that applies to bath
water just as well as drinking water.

200
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,880
One question first.

201
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:15,402
Robi, perchance were you able to
collect any valuable information?

202
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:18,020
I'm afraid not.

203
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:20,797
Though I'll share my meager scraps.

204
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:23,777
I know what time Orochi will
wake up on the day of the battle.

205
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:27,237
I know what offerings they will
take with them to Onigashima.

206
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:30,377
I know Kaido's favorite food
and his crew's hierarchy.

207
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:33,166
And the number of soldiers
and weapons that...

208
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:35,020
That's meager?

209
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:38,300
By the way, I happened upon a poneglyph.

210
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:41,920
Alas, it wasn't a red one, though. Really?

211
00:10:42,260 --> 00:10:44,966
You're two for two on
finding those, Bonkichi.

212
00:10:45,260 --> 00:10:47,937
It was in a basement room
with a reinforced door.

213
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:50,640
An odd place full of wooden dolls.

214
00:10:51,340 --> 00:10:55,037
There should be a road poneglyph
here, but if it's not in the castle,

215
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:57,061
we can assume it's on Onigashima.

216
00:10:57,580 --> 00:10:58,756
Kaido's Island, huh?

217
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:00,930
Splendid.

218
00:11:01,013 --> 00:11:03,617
We've acquired a treasure
Traffy of information.

219
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:05,876
The mission was a resounding success.

220
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:08,140
I thank you all.

221
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:11,880
To have such reliable
allies is truly a gift.

222
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:14,957
Since all that's settled, let's go.

223
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:18,628
We'll have a nice healing bath
and also see some panties, OK?

224
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:21,620
You'll stand out and
you're a pervert! What?

225
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,220
Breaking news!

226
00:11:23,620 --> 00:11:28,337
Everyone's favorite Oiran, Komurasaki, met
a terrible fate at the Shogun's Banquet.

227
00:11:28,420 --> 00:11:31,457
There was a big disagreement
and Kyoshiro cut her right down.

228
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:32,370
No lie!

229
00:11:32,453 --> 00:11:34,960
Find out more right here! Don't be shy!

230
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:41,530
Komurasaki!

231
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:49,757
Don't you think you're
being a bit dramatic?

232
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:51,300
You only saw her once.

233
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:54,377
The whole world should mourn
the death of a beauty like her.

234
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:56,166
Seems the funeral's tomorrow.

235
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:58,046
You're heartless, all of you!

236
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:00,720
My raid suit?

237
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:03,857
You don't think Odobee and
the others got caught, do you?

238
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:04,900
I'm worried.

239
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:08,497
Do you think I should try
to contact them by smell?

240
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:10,051
What do you think, Sanji?

241
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,024
I know where to use this power.

242
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:15,017
I'll go to the women's bath.

243
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:16,137
It's my dream.

244
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:17,120
Hey, Sanji!

245
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:18,340
So much skin.

246
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:22,200
Right, whatever Usopp just said.

247
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:25,837
By the way, Traffy, is there
anything about Udon in the paper?

248
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:27,214
About Lufitaro, maybe?

249
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:28,620
Bet there is.

250
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:31,977
If he hasn't gone on a rampage
yet, it's only a matter of time.

251
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:33,217
I hope you're right.

252
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:34,677
I just can't wait to see him.

253
